                "reply_count": 1,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "I met with Hawai\u2019i Director of Human Services Ryan Yamane and his dedicated team to stay aligned on the federal administration\u2019s cruel intent to withhold payments to states starting November for SNAP, the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program that provides crucial food and nutrition assistance to some 165,000 of our \u2018ohana throughout Hawai\u2019i. The admin is blaming it on the shutdown but it has a $5 billion contingency fund and can move other funds to cover SNAP for November (here\u2019s my letter with colleagues to the Agriculture Secretary to release these funds). The State of Hawai\u2019i has a plan to help if the administration actually cuts this critical funding; info: https://t.co/EjNY73wr3v",
